    "module_designation": null,
    "description": "The CDI-1600 is a self-indicating, mains-powered indicator designed to be used as part of a single range, single or dual-scale, Class III or IIII, non-automatic weighing instrument. Features: stainless steel enclosure fitted with panel mount bracket or tilt stand; colour LCD display; 27-button keypad (5 function keys, 5 primary scale function keys, 4 navigation keys, enter key, 12-key numeric keypad); connections and ports located on the bottom face. Devices: semi-automatic zero setting, zero tracking, semi-automatic subtractive tare weighing, preset tare, zero indicator, indication of stable equilibrium, gross/net/tare display, single or dual-scale, totalisation, display check at power up, printing. Interfaces: 6-wire load cell connection, RS232/RS485, Ethernet, USB, digital I/O, PS/2. Legally relevant software designated version V2.xx.xx; legally relevant parameters (Service menu) accessible only via calibration switch on the CPU board. Access to load cell connection(s) and calibration switch is prevented by sealing the enclosure (wire-and-seal or tamper-evident sticker with securing mark)."
